[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:The Best and the Worst]
[00:03.92]Why is Joe's garden | 为什么乔的花园
[00:11.97]the most beautiful one in the town? | 是镇上最漂亮的一个？
[00:15.78]Joe Sanders has the most beautiful garden | 乔·桑德斯拥有最美丽的花园
[00:20.56]in our town. | 在我们镇上。
[00:21.96]Nearly everybody enters for | 几乎每个人都报名参加
[00:25.00]'The Nicest Garden Competition' each year, | 每年的“最美花园竞赛”，
[00:28.84]but Joe wins every time. | 但乔每次都赢。
[00:32.42]Bill Frith's garden is larger than Joe's. | 比尔·弗里斯的花园比乔的花园大。
[00:36.36]Bill works harder than Joe | 比尔比乔更努力工作
[00:38.76]and grows more flowers and vegetables, | 并且种植更多的花卉和蔬菜，
[00:41.90]but Joe's garden is more interesting. | 但乔的花园更有趣。
[00:45.46]He has made neat paths | 他修建了整齐的小径
[00:47.86]and has built a wooden bridge over a pool. | 并在池塘上架起了一座木桥。
[00:51.40]I like gardens too, | 我也喜欢花园，
[00:54.18]but I do not like hard work. | 但我不喜欢辛苦劳作。
[00:57.60]Every year | 每年
[00:58.93]I enter for the garden competition too, | 我也参加花园竞赛，
[01:02.44]and I always win a little prize | 我总是赢得一个小奖
[01:05.80]for the worst garden in the town! | 因为我是镇上最差的花园！